# Bandit baseline for Phantom (a dual-use, authorised red-team framework).
#
# The security-scan CI job now FAILS on any HIGH-severity finding NOT listed
# here. These five are reviewed and accepted BY DESIGN, not silently ignored:
#
#   B324  weak hashlib (md5/sha1) — used only for NON-security identifiers
#         (stable cache/record keys), never for signatures or password hashing.
#   B501  requests with verify=False — talking to the operator's OWN C2 with a
#         self-signed certificate, inside an authorised engagement.
#   B602  subprocess with shell=True — the documented pipeline execution path;
#         the interpolation boundary is validated (safe_exec / target checks).
#   B402  import ftplib — used by exploit/PoC modules for the FTP service.
#   B321  ftplib.FTP — same; a red-team tool must be able to speak FTP.
#
# Anything else at HIGH severity is a regression and should FAIL the scan.
skips:
  - B324
  - B501
  - B602
  - B402
  - B321
